					<h3>Privacy Features</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>GDPR compliant</li>
						<li>No tracking cookies</li>
						<li>No search history</li>
						<li>Qwant Junior for kids</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>EU privacy laws apply</li>
								<li>No AI by default</li>
								<li>Good for European content</li>
								<li>Kid-safe version</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Weaker for US content</li>
								<li>Partially relies on Bing</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/qwant-search-engine" class="learn-more">Learn more about Qwant &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="mojeek">
				<h2>Mojeek</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag">Fully Independent</span>
							<span class="engine-tag green">No AI</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>UK-based search engine with a completely independent index. No reliance on Google, Bing, or any other search provider.</p>

					<h3>Privacy Features</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Own crawler and index</li>
						<li>No tracking whatsoever</li>
						<li>Transparent ranking algorithm</li>
						<li>No filter bubbles</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>100% independent</li>
								<li>No tracking at all</li>
								<li>Transparent ranking</li>
								<li>No AI features</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Smaller index</li>
								<li>Results less comprehensive</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/mojeek-search-engine" class="learn-more">Learn more about Mojeek &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="presearch">
				<h2>Presearch</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag">Decentralized</span>
							<span class="engine-tag green">No AI</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>Decentralized search engine that aggregates results from multiple sources. Earn crypto tokens for searching.</p>

					<h3>Privacy Features</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Decentralized infrastructure</li>
						<li>No central data storage</li>
						<li>Community-driven</li>
						<li>Open source</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Truly decentralized</li>
								<li>Earn PRE tokens</li>
								<li>Multiple sources</li>
								<li>No AI</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Results can vary</li>
								<li>Less polished interface</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/presearch-search-engine" class="learn-more">Learn more about Presearch &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="faq">
				<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What is the best private search engine?</h3>
					<p>It depends on your priorities. For the best results, use <a href="/guides/startpage-search-engine">Startpage</a> (Google results without tracking). For full independence, use <a href="/guides/mojeek-search-engine">Mojeek</a> or Brave Search. For the best balance, <a href="/guides/duckduckgo-vs-google">DuckDuckGo</a> is a solid choice.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is DuckDuckGo really private?</h3>
					<p>Yes. DuckDuckGo doesn't store your searches, IP address, or any personal information. However, they use Bing's index, which means Microsoft sees anonymized queries. For complete independence, consider Mojeek or Brave Search.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Which search engine doesn't track you?</h3>
					<p>All engines on this page have no-tracking policies: DuckDuckGo, Startpage, Brave Search, Qwant, Mojeek, and Presearch. The most verifiable are Mojeek and Brave, which use their own independent indexes.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Startpage better than DuckDuckGo for privacy?</h3>
					<p>Both are excellent for privacy. Startpage is based in the Netherlands (better privacy laws) and provides Google results. DuckDuckGo is US-based and uses Bing. Startpage's Anonymous View feature gives it an edge for browsing privacy.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Do private search engines have AI features?</h3>
					<p>Most don't. Startpage, Qwant, Mojeek, and Presearch have no AI features. DuckDuckGo and Brave have optional AI that can be disabled. Use <a href="/">Unslop Search</a> to automatically disable AI across all engines.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<div class="next-steps">
				<h2>Next Steps</h2>
				<div class="next-links">
